      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface biotinylation and immunoblot analysis confirmed V5-tagged eAE1 is present at the plasma membrane (PMC11769940, Figure 2). Anion-transport function NOT MEASURED for the V5-tagged construct per ledger.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "PMC11769940 explicitly shows the construct sequence for V5-tagged eAE1: the V5 tag (GKPIPNPLLGLDST) is flanked by YNVL on the N-terminal side and MVPK on the C-terminal side. Python computation on the canonical sequence confirms YNVL = positions 555-558 (Y555, N556, V557, L558) and MVPK = positions 559-562 (M559, V560, P561, K562), pinning the insertion junction to after L558 (insert_after_residue=558). This is 1 residue C-terminal of the HA/Myc site (557). Both sites are within EL3 (542-569), >=3 aa from both TM boundaries, with no glycosylation motifs or cysteines in EL3. Surface biotinylation confirmed plasma membrane localization of the V5-tagged construct. [validation: surface_only; position: inferred; source: paper; entailment_verified: True]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 39872416,
          "citation": "PMID 39872416",
          "claim": "The cells were transfected with human wt-kAE1 containing a V5 tag inserted into extracellular loop 3 (EL3; 490\u2013YNVL GKPIPNPLLGLDST MVPK\u2013511), human wt-eAE1 containing a V5 tag inserted into extracellular loop 3 (EL3; 555\u2013YNVL GKPIPNPLLGLDST MVPK\u2013576) or an empty pcDNA3.1(+) expression vector (mock transfected)."
        }
      ],
